<title>FRANCE: Details of new EU negative grain correctives.</title>
<headline>Details of new EU negative grain correctives.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union has introduced correctives to discourage grain exports at the turn of the season -- a routine measure but especially vital this year to prevent new-crop southern barley being sold with old-crop licences valid in June, trade sources said.</p>
<p>The barrier for June barley is necessary as Spain is unusually competitive on the world market using normal EU restitutions and its crop arrives in June.</p>
<p>The EU's management committee in Brussels on Thursday set a 20 Ecu per tonne negative corrective on refunds for barley exports in June and July, the sources said.</p>
<p>Other negative correctives were 10 Ecus for durum in June and July, 10 Ecus for soft wheat in July only, 20 Ecus for oats in July, 10 Ecus for rye in July, 10 Ecus for soft wheat and rye flour in July and 15 Ecus for durum groats in June and July.</p>
